Subject: [PATCH v2] mail: Add just commit-mail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: ppvulnkkwnrpxzusskntwqrloyrlnllu

Mail delivered into the maildir lands in the working copy alongside
flag renames and edits, and each new message is committed on its own
by hand as "mail: <subject>". Copying subjects by hand is slow and
lets stray characters slip into the log.

commit-mail takes every file added under maildir/ in @ and commits it
alone, named for its Subject header, so a batch of new mail becomes
one reviewable commit per message. Renamed and edited files stay in
the working copy, since a flag change or an archive move is not a new
message. The prefix defaults to the "mail: " every message commit
carries today and can be given as an argument:

    just commit-mail 'just: '

The subject is read from the header only, after joining folded lines.
Long subjects are folded onto a second line, as git format-patch and
notmuch reply both do, and taking only the first line would cut the
commit subject short. Stopping at the blank line that ends the header
keeps a "Subject:" line in a body or a quoted message from being
taken instead.
---
This applies to the mail branch, not trunk; base-commit is
mail@upstream. Like "[PATCH] mail: Add just archive" [1] it appends to
the Justfile, so whichever lands second needs a trivial rebase.

Tested in a scratch jj repo: three added files (a plain message, a
copy of a list message whose Subject is folded onto two lines, and
one whose only "Subject:" line is in the body) became three commits
named "mail: plain one", the full unfolded subject, and "mail: (no
subject)". A rename and an edit in the same working copy stayed
uncommitted. A prefix given as an argument, run from maildir/, was
used as given.

Changes in v2:
- Find added files with `jj st maildir` and awk instead of a jj diff
  template, as Pat asked.
- Read the subject with sed from an unfolded header instead of one
  awk program that both parses and joins. A grep for the first
  "subject:" line alone would truncate folded subjects, which occur
  on the list.
- Drop CR handling; maildir-deliver.sh writes LF line endings and no
  message on the list has a CR.
- Quiet the jj commit in the recipe, to match the other recipes in
  "mail: Quiet the just tasks"; the recipe now prints nothing on
  success.
- Link to v1: id:4a1774d25df53c3c75f89f63c200fbb4594aec62.1791650481.git.claude@p7x.dev

